=== §19's questions, asked of two configurations of the SAME process


                        cells  fires  caught the real one  false alarms
  by region x category  12     1      false                1
  plus store            60     1      true                 0

  The coarse configuration MISSES the collapse it exists to find,
  and the one time it does fire, it is wrong. Every alarm it raises
  in a year is a false one. The fine configuration catches the real
  event and raises nothing else.

  Same code, same data, same year. Nothing in the source says which
  of the two you have -- only the replay does, which is why R5 makes
  it a precondition rather than a feature to add later.

=== the gates, with the fine configuration's rehearsal

  within authority, never rehearsed         REFUSED  this process has never been replayed against history, so nothing is known about how often it fires or how often it is wrong (design R5)
  within authority, rehearsed               acts     within delegated authority
  beyond authority, rehearsed, unapproved   REFUSED  this recommendation exceeds the delegated authority and no approval is on file: cost 15000 exceeds the spend limit of 5000
  beyond authority, rehearsed, approved     acts     approved by regional director

  Note the first line. An unrehearsed process is refused BEFORE
  authority is even considered, and approval does not substitute:
  a human asked to approve it has nothing to approve on, because
  nobody knows how often it fires or how often it is wrong.
